(1)\">.","ownWords.whatIDo":"I fix bicycles at your house, usually the same week.","beFound.searchedFor":"\"bike repair near me\", probably. Richard says to leave this alone for now."},"submissions":[{"conceptId":"scoping-what-to-build","attempt":1,"submittedAt":"2026-09-07T21:12:00.000Z","evaluated":true,"deliverableId":"obj-scope"},{"conceptId":"what-the-web-is","attempt":1,"submittedAt":"2026-09-06T19:20:00.000Z","evaluated":true,"deliverableId":null}],"work":[{"source":"artifact","submissionId":"what-the-web-is:1","conceptId":"what-the-web-is","sectionId":"web-16","assignmentId":null,"attempt":1,"submittedAt":"2026-09-06T19:20:00.000Z","content":"When you type my address, your phone sends a message to a computer somewhere else — that's where my page actually lives. That computer sends a copy of the page back, and your phone puts it on your screen, photos and all. So what you're looking at is your own copy. The real one stays where it is, and if I change it, the next person gets the new one. If you fill in the form and press Send, your message goes back across to that computer, and it passes it on to my email. I don't see anything until it lands in my inbox.","linkUrl":null,"evaluation":{"criteria":[{"name":"Says their phone or computer asks for the page, and a computer somewhere else sends it back","status":"met","note":"\"Your phone sends a message to a computer somewhere else… that computer sends a copy of the page back\" — the whole exchange, in words a customer would follow."},{"name":"Makes clear that what they see is a copy, and the original stays where the page is hosted","status":"met","note":"\"What you're looking at is your own copy. The real one stays where it is\" answers the question most people get stuck on, and the line about the next person getting the new one shows you really have it."},{"name":"Explains that pressing Send makes a message travel away from their phone to something that passes it to your inbox","status":"partly","note":"The messag