essage without phoning\" — one sentence, one real person, one thing they do."},{"name":"Lists what is on the page, and the list stops at four things or fewer","status":"met","note":"Four things, and you stopped at four."},{"name":"Has a “not yet” list with at least two things on it that you genuinely wanted","status":"met","note":"Booking is on it, and you say you would love it. That is the one that counts: cutting something you did not want is easy."},{"name":"Names at least one assumption that would change the approach if it were wrong","status":"partly","note":"You named a good one: that people would rather write than ring. Say what you would put on the page if it turns out wrong, and it becomes a decision instead of a worry."},{"name":"Contains no technical words that you could not explain to a friend","status":"met","note":"Nothing here you could not say to a customer. \"Form\" is the most technical word in it, and everyone knows what that is."}],"summary":"This is a boundary you can actually hold Claude Code to: one job, four things, and a \"not yet\" list with something on it you genuinely wanted. The assumption you picked is the right one to keep an eye on.","nextEdit":"Add one line under the assumption: what goes on the page instead if most people would rather phone."}},{"source":"assignment","submissionId":"sub-brief-scope","conceptId":null,"sectionId":null,"assignmentId":"brief-scope","attempt":1,"submittedAt":"2026-09-07T21:12:00.000Z","content":"**My scope note — version one**\n\n**The one job.** A stranger with a broken bike finds my page, believes I'm real, and sends me a message without phoning.\n\n**What's on the page.**\n- What I do, in one sentence\n- Where I cover — about ten miles round town\n- Six photos of bikes I've fixed\n- A form: their name, how to reach them, and what's wrong with the bike\n\n**Not yet.**\n- Online booking. I'd love it, but it means my real diary, cancellations, and people turning up when I'm not there.\n- Prices. They depend on the bike.\n- A blog. I won't keep it up and an empty one looks worse than none.\n\n**The assumption.** That people would rather write to me than ring. If most of them would rather phone, the form isn't the main thing — my number is.","linkUrl":null,"evaluation":null}],"onboardingFacts":[{"key":"projectGoal","label":"What they want to build or understand"},{"key":"buildOrUnderstand","label":"Whether they are building a thing or making sense of one"},{"key":"currentSkillLevel","label":"Where they are starting from"},{"key":"stackOrTools","label":"Tools, stack or environment already in play"}]}]/*FIXTURE-END*/;
